text I'm at Kotomi's house holding an armload of tools.
text White paint, paint thinner, rust-proofing chemicals.
text A paint brush, a wire brush, sandpaper.
text I was at the paint store at eight in the morning buying all of this stuff.
text I said I wanted to paint a garden chair and the clerk told me what I needed and how to do it.
text Of course, this time I prepared a change of clothes and work gloves.
text I thought about everything when I got home last night.
text And I made up my mind.
text No more indecision. I'll do everything I can.
text The steps I'm taking are that important.
text That's what I've decided to believe.
