text I move the chairs and table to a corner of the garden.
text I assess the table's condition.
text In my memories, it's painted bright white.
text The table's paint is now flaking off and rust is everywhere. Exposed metal is showing in lots of places.
text I take the wire brush and scrape off the large patches of rust.
text Smaller patches of rust get the sandpaper.
text When the bare metal starts to appear, I apply the rust-proofing chemicals.
text I'm completely immersed in the work.
