text It takes me about an hour to finish rust-proofing the table.
text While it dries, I start on a chair.
text I initially thought these would be easier because they're smaller, but their complicated shape makes them even harder to deal with.
text The second chair gets the same treatment with the sandpaper before I finish rust-proofing it.
text I decide to trim the hedges and trees while the chairs dry.
text I take the hedge clippers to a branch and squeeze with all my might.
text I hear a snapping sound and lots of green leaves fall to the ground.
text While I continue to work near the edge of the garden, I see something.
text @[Tomoya]
text Oops.
text Something hits my fingertips as I'm weeding and I jump backward.
text At first I think it's a stone, but it's a dirty, blackened brick.
text Bricks buried in the soil form a ring-shaped barrier blocking off the weeds.
text @[Tomoya]
text I get it...
text As if part of the scab in my mind flakes away, some memories return.
text This is that flower bed.
text Many varieties of colorful flowers filled this area.
text I feel like I just discovered the ruins of an ancient city.
text I remove the overgrown weeds.
text A small bug scurries away, frightened by the light suddenly shining on it.
setvar strS[1000] = "SIRO"
