text Once the rust-proofing dries, it's time for the paint.
text I open the can of paint and dip the brush into it.
text I try to apply the paint as evenly as possible.
text The sky is clear; it's the perfect day for painting.
text It makes me want to whistle while I work.
text I never imagined I would spend a Sunday painting in a garden.
text The legs of the chairs are spotty from the rust-proofing. Returning them to pure whiteness with new paint is a great feeling.
text If Kotomi were here, it'd be all the more fun.
text @[Tomoya]
text Well, she'd probably just get in the way.
text She'd mess with the tools and get covered in paint. I can already see it happening.
text There's no need to hurry.
text Kotomi will get her chance to do some gardening.
