text The town is unchanging.
text The babbling of the crowds and the exhaust of the cars.
text The store signs and window displays flood my senses.
text It feels like I came from a different world that smells of earth, grass, and paint.
text I head to the bookstore first.
text I skim some books in the gardening section.
text Every single page has a lot of useful information.
text I learn that the way I sharpened the clippers was totally wrong.
text Moreover, those clippers are for hedge trimming and not for cutting grass.
text It says here that grass shouldn't be cut without planning. Rotted patches should be replaced.
text @[Tomoya]
text I'm doing everything wrong.
text I'm at a loss.
text I buy a beginner's book on gardening and one on garden flowers.
text Then I walk over to the usual fast food shop.
text I get a burger combo with a coffee and find a place to sit.
text Delving into the books, I start making a list of all the things I'll need to buy and do.
text .........
text ......
text ...
