text It's midnight.
text The May darkness feels sticky.
text Insects are incessantly chirping.
text The grass smells of the evening dew.
text I'm still digging in the dirt.
text The goal is to replace the soil of the flower bed.
text There's no light here. What little I can see is due to the starlight.
text I stick the shovel into the dirt and put my weight into it.
text *Crunch* *Crunch* *Crunch*
text It feels like I'm digging up a corpse.
text The memories of my childhood are probably buried under here.
text I wipe away the sweat and turn to look at the house.
text The roof is high off the ground, as if hovering above me.
text Glints of light reflect off the jet black, mirror-like windows.
text Is Kotomi asleep?
text Can she sleep right now?
text Is she having a bad dream?
text I have no answers.
text I glare at the darkness and keep digging.
text *Crunch* *Crunch* *Crunch*
text All the worries I kept trapped inside during the day are inching their way up my body, starting from the soles of my shoes.
text When I find out that all of this is for nothing...
text When not a single thing I believe in comes to pass...
text What will I do then?
text Will I be able to withstand it?
text I don't know.
